       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **What was written:** 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The labeled maximum for metformin IR is 2,550 mg/day. Single doses are usually 500\u20131,000 mg, and 850 mg is common. This order is 3 times the daily maximum, and each dose alone equals the whole daily maximum. That raises the risk of severe lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **2,550 mg total per day**, divided in some other way, such as 1,275 mg twice daily. Another option is 1,000 mg twice daily, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 2550 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. Give me a clinical rationale to add to the order note too."
